'''Crokind Shand''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] from the [[planet]] [[Nar Kanji]] who served as a member of the criminal [[Kanjiklub]] gang around thirty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]]. He accompanied the gang's [[topboss]], [[Tasu Leech]], and several other members in boarding the [[Baleen-class heavy freighter|''Baleen''-class heavy freighter]] ''[[Eravana]]'' in order to reclaim 50,000 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] owed to the Kanjiklub by the vessel's owner, the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]].

==Biography==
Crokind Shand was [[Reproduction|born]] on the [[planet]] [[Nar Kanji]]<ref name="TFAVD" /> and became a pit-fighter. Injuries caused him to lose an [[eye]] and his [[Limb|right leg]], and he began wearing an eyepatch and [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] right leg.<ref name="Databank" /> Later in his life, he became a member of [[Tasu Leech]]'s criminal gang [[Kanjiklub]]. At some point of his life, [[Corellian]] [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] got into debt with Kanjklub, owing them 50,000 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|VII}} to [[34 ABY]].</ref> Shand accompanied Leech and the other Kanjiklub members to Solo's [[Starship|vessel]] the [[Baleen-class heavy freighter|''Baleen''-class heavy freighter]] ''[[Eravana]]'' to reclaim the 50,000 credits that Solo owed them. The Kanjiklub arrived in the [[freighter]]'s airlock shortly after the [[Guavian Death Gang]], who Solo also owed money, and the smuggler found himself trapped between the two groups. As Leech and [[Bala-Tik]], frontman for the Death Squad, argued with Solo, the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] and the former [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] [[Finn]], who Solo had recently brought aboard, accidentally released three [[rathtar]]s that were being kept on the ship. The creatures immediately attacked the two criminal groups, and in the ensuing [[Skirmish aboard the Eravana|chaos]],<ref name="TFA" /> Shand was eaten by the rathtars along with all of his comrades,<ref name="Helmet Collection" /> while Solo and his companions managed to escape the creatures on board the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''.<ref name="TFA" />

==Personality and traits==
As a hard-bitten member of the Kanjiklub gang, Crokind Shand was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who wore an eyepatch and a [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] right [[Limb|leg]] rigged to deliver fierce kicks. He had tanned skin and black [[hair]].<ref name="TFAVD" /> His missing [[eye]] and right leg were injuries that he suffered during his career as a pit-fighter. His appearance offered ample evidence that messing with him would be a potentially fatal mistake.<ref name="Databank" />

==Equipment==
In battle he used a [[heavy bore rifle]] with a reinforced-[[galven circuit]] [[barrel]] with a makeshift [[bayonet]] attached to it with brown cord and a [[roggwart]] [[bone]] [[Stock|rifle butt]]. A [[Captain Ithano's blaster rifle|visually identical weapon]] was also used by the [[pirate]] captain [[Sidon Ithano]] after he had captured it from another Kanjiklubber.<ref name="TFAVD" />

==Behind the scenes==
Crokind Shand first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], which was released in North America on [[December 18]], [[2015]].<ref name="TFA" /> The character was not named in the film, but received identification in ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]'', a reference book written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] and released in conjunction with the film.<ref name="TFAVD" /> He was portrayed by [[Cecep Arif Rahman]] in the film,<ref name="BBC">{{WebCite|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-35131428|text=Iko Uwais and the Indonesian heroes of Star Wars: The Force Awakens|date=2015-12-18|work=[[Wikipedia:BBC|BBC]]|archivedate=20191010161158}}</ref> but his role was not listed in the end credits.<ref name="TFA" /> Rahman and his fellow Kanjiklub actors [[Yayan Ruhian]] and [[Iko Uwais]], also appeared together in the [[Wikipedia:Indonesia|Indonesian]] action thrillers [[Wikipedia:The Raid (2011 film)|''The Raid'']] and [[Wikipedia:The Raid 2|''The Raid 2'']].<ref name="BBC" />

